IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `vcat-dates`
IMPORT `vcat-party`

-- Victorian Civil and Administrative Tribunal Act 1998 -- worked cases for the party's questions (vcat-party.l4) and the
-- date helpers. Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the encoding's
-- output. Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. The facts are illustrative.
-- Month lengths used: February 2026 and 2027 have 28 days, February 2024 and 2028 have 29.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`
`TAC review` MEANS `a review of a decision under section 77 of the Transport Accident Act 1986`
`TAC other` MEANS `another proceeding under the Transport Accident Act 1986`
`small claim` MEANS `a proceeding relating to a small claim under the Australian Consumer Law and Fair Trading Act 2012`
`EO` MEANS `a proceeding under the Equal Opportunity Act 2010`
`building` MEANS `a domestic building work dispute under the Domestic Building Contracts Act 1995`
`owners or planning` MEANS `a proceeding under the Owners Corporations Act 2006 (other than a review under its section 191), under section 114, 120 or 149A of the Planning and Environment Act 1987, or of a kind prescribed for section 115C`
`review` MEANS `a review of a decision under another enabling enactment`
`original` MEANS `another proceeding in VCAT's original jurisdiction`

§§ `Dates`

#ASSERT `the date` 28 `days after` (`d` 3 8 2026) EQUALS `d` 31 8 2026
#ASSERT `the date` 30 `days after` (`d` 2 2 2026) EQUALS `d` 4 3 2026
#ASSERT `the same day` 12 `months after` (`d` 29 2 2024) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2025
#ASSERT `the same day` 12 `months after` (`d` 15 3 2025) EQUALS `d` 15 3 2026
#ASSERT `the days from` (`d` 1 7 2026) `to` (`d` 30 8 2026) EQUALS 60

§§ `ss 40-42 -- jurisdiction`

#ASSERT `Which jurisdiction is my proceeding in` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `review jurisdiction: VCAT reviews a decision made by a decision-maker, with all the decision-maker's functions (ss 42(1), 48, 51)`
#ASSERT `Which jurisdiction is my proceeding in` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `original jurisdiction: VCAT decides the matter itself under the enabling enactment (ss 41, 43, 44)`
-- s 42(2): Part 7 of the Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 is original even if it reviews something.
#ASSERT `Which jurisdiction is my proceeding in` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `original jurisdiction: VCAT decides the matter itself under the enabling enactment (ss 41, 43, 44)`

