-- Notice received 15 January 2027: lodge by 12 February 2027.
#ASSERT `By when must the decision-maker lodge the material` (`d` 15 1 2027) EQUALS `d` 12 2 2027

§§ `s 50 -- the decision during the review`

#ASSERT `Does the decision operate during the review` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: starting the review does not affect the decision; it keeps operating and can be put into effect unless VCAT stays it (s 50(1), (3))`
#ASSERT `Does the decision operate during the review` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: VCAT has made an order staying the decision (s 50(2)(b), (3))`
#ASSERT `Does the decision operate during the review` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not covered: the enabling enactment provides otherwise; its own rule decides (s 50(2)(a))`

§§ `ss 51(5), 99(2) -- missing the hearing`

#ASSERT `What happens if I miss the hearing` `TAC review` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `VCAT must confirm the decision under review (s 51(5))`
-- s 51(5) has no notice condition (finding 2).
#ASSERT `What happens if I miss the hearing` `review` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `VCAT must confirm the decision under review (s 51(5))`
#ASSERT `What happens if I miss the hearing` `review` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `does not arise: I appeared, personally or by a representative`
#ASSERT `What happens if I miss the hearing` `review` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the hearing may be held in my absence, as I was given notice of it in accordance with the rules (s 99(2))`
#ASSERT `What happens if I miss the hearing` `small claim` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the hearing may be held in my absence, as I was given notice of it in accordance with the rules (s 99(2))`
#ASSERT `What happens if I miss the hearing` `EO` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered: s 99(2) speaks only of a person given notice in accordance with the rules`

