-- s 112, from the seat of the party who made the offer and (mirror) of the party who did not accept it: same facts, same answer.
`entitled` MEANS `yes: the party who did not accept the offer must pay all the costs the party who made it incurred after the offer was made (s 112(2))`
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to costs after my offer was rejected` `original` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 14 FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `entitled`
#ASSERT `Must I pay costs after rejecting an offer` `original` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 14 FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `entitled`
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to costs after my offer was rejected` `TAC review` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 14 FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `entitled`
#ASSERT `Must I pay costs after rejecting an offer` `TAC review` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 14 FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `entitled`
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to costs after my offer was rejected` `review` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 14 FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: section 112 does not apply to a proceeding for review of a decision (s 112(1)(a))`
#ASSERT `Must I pay costs after rejecting an offer` `review` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 14 FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: section 112 does not apply to a proceeding for review of a decision (s 112(1)(a))`
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to costs after my offer was rejected` `EO` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 14 FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not covered: sections 112 to 115 do not apply to a proceeding under the Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Sch 1 cl 22)`
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to costs after my offer was rejected` `small claim` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 14 FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: VCAT cannot order costs in a proceeding relating to a small claim (Sch 1 cl 4I(1))`
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to costs after my offer was rejected` `building` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 13 FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: the offer was not in writing, or does not comply with sections 113 and 114 (s 112(1)(a), (c))`
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to costs after my offer was rejected` `building` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 14 FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: the offer was not in writing, or does not comply with sections 113 and 114 (s 112(1)(a), (c))`
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to costs after my offer was rejected` `building` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 14 FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: the offer was not in writing, or does not comply with sections 113 and 114 (s 112(1)(a), (c))`
#ASSERT `Must I pay costs after rejecting an offer` `building` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 14 TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: the offer was accepted while it was open (s 112(1)(b))`
#ASSERT `Must I pay costs after rejecting an offer` `building` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 14 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: in VCAT's opinion its orders are more favourable to the party who did not accept than the offer (s 112(1)(d))`
#ASSERT `Must I pay costs after rejecting an offer` `building` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 14 FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: VCAT has ordered otherwise (s 112(2))`

#ASSERT `What can VCAT do if an accepted offer is not kept` `original` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `VCAT may, at my request, give effect to the terms of the offer, or dismiss the proceeding (s 115(1)(a), (b)(i))`
#ASSERT `What can VCAT do if an accepted offer is not kept` `original` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `VCAT may, at my request, give effect to the terms of the offer, dismiss the proceeding, or award me any or all of what I asked for in my counterclaim (s 115(1)(a), (b))`
#ASSERT `What can VCAT do if an accepted offer is not kept` `TAC review` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `VCAT may, at my request, give effect to the terms of the offer, or award me any or all of what I asked for in my application (s 115(1)(a), (c))`
#ASSERT `What can VCAT do if an accepted offer is not kept` `original` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `VCAT may, at my request, make an order giving effect to the terms of the offer (s 115(1)(a))`
#ASSERT `What can VCAT do if an accepted offer is not kept` `EO` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not covered: sections 112 to 115 do not apply to a proceeding under the Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Sch 1 cl 22)`

§§ `ss 109, 115C, Sch 1 cls 4I, 12B, 92 -- costs and fees`

#ASSERT `Will I have to pay the other party's costs` `original` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: each party bears their own costs, as VCAT is not satisfied that it is fair to order otherwise (s 109(1), (3))`
#ASSERT `Will I have to pay the other party's costs` `EO` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `possibly: VCAT may order me to pay all or a specified part of another party's costs, as it is satisfied that it is fair to do so (s 109(2), (3))`
#ASSERT `Will I have to pay the other party's costs` `TAC review` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not covered: section 109 does not apply to a proceeding under the Transport Accident Act 1986 (Sch 1 cl 92); costs follow that Act`
#ASSERT `Will I have to pay the other party's costs` `TAC other` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered: section 109 does not apply to a proceeding under the Transport Accident Act 1986 (Sch 1 cl 92); costs follow that Act`
#ASSERT `Will I have to pay the other party's costs` `small claim` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: VCAT cannot order costs in a proceeding relating to a small claim (Sch 1 cl 4I(1))`
#ASSERT `Will I have to pay the other party's costs` `small claim` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `possibly: VCAT may order me to pay all or a specified part of another party's costs, as it is satisfied that it is fair to do so (s 109(2), (3))`
#ASSERT `Will I have to pay the other party's costs` `building` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: VCAT must award costs against me, as I was unsuccessful and refused, or did not in good faith take part in, the conciliation conference the dispute was referred to (Sch 1 cl 12B(2))`
#ASSERT `Will I have to pay the other party's costs` `building` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: each party bears their own costs, as VCAT is not satisfied that it is fair to order otherwise (s 109(1), (3))`
#ASSERT `Will I have to pay the other party's costs` `building` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: each party bears their own costs, as VCAT is not satisfied that it is fair to order otherwise (s 109(1), (3))`
#ASSERT `Will I have to pay the other party's costs` `building` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `possibly: VCAT may order me to pay all or a specified part of another party's costs, as it is satisfied that it is fair to do so (s 109(2), (3))`

#ASSERT `Do I get my fees back` `small claim` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: I am entitled to an order that the other party reimburse me the whole of the fees I paid in the proceeding (s 115C(2))`
#ASSERT `Do I get my fees back` `building` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: I am entitled to an order that the other party reimburse me the whole of the fees I paid in the proceeding (s 115C(2))`
#ASSERT `Do I get my fees back` `owners or planning` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: VCAT has ordered otherwise, having regard to the proceeding and the parties' conduct (s 115C(3))`
#ASSERT `Do I get my fees back` `small claim` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no presumption: I did not substantially succeed against the other party (s 115C(2))`
#ASSERT `Do I get my fees back` `EO` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no presumption in this kind of proceeding: VCAT may still order the other party to reimburse my fees, having regard to the proceeding, the parties' conduct and the result (s 115B)`
#ASSERT `Do I get my fees back` `TAC review` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no presumption in this kind of proceeding: VCAT may still order the other party to reimburse my fees, having regard to the proceeding, the parties' conduct and the result (s 115B)`

