#ASSERT `By when must VCAT give written reasons` (`d` 16 7 2026) 0 EQUALS `d` 30 8 2026
#ASSERT `By when must VCAT give written reasons` (`d` 16 7 2026) 15 EQUALS `d` 14 9 2026

#ASSERT `Can I have an order made in my absence re-opened` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: I am not a person in respect of whom the order was made (s 120(1))`
#ASSERT `Can I have an order made in my absence re-opened` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: I appeared or was represented at the hearing at which the order was made (s 120(1))`
#ASSERT `Can I have an order made in my absence re-opened` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `I may apply (within the time the rules set), but VCAT will not hear it unless satisfied that I had a reasonable excuse for not attending or being represented (s 120(4)(a)(i))`
#ASSERT `Can I have an order made in my absence re-opened` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `I may apply (within the time the rules set), but VCAT will not hear it unless satisfied that it is appropriate to, having regard to whether I have a reasonable case and any prejudice to another party (s 120(4)(a)(ii), (4A), (4B))`
#ASSERT `Can I have an order made in my absence re-opened` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `I may apply, and VCAT may hear the application and, if it thinks fit, revoke or vary the order; it may require an undertaking as to costs or damages (s 120(4), (4C))`

-- An illustrative Magistrates' Court limit of $100 000: at the limit and a dollar over.
#ASSERT `Where can I enforce my VCAT order` TRUE 100000 100000 EQUALS `in the Magistrates' Court, as the amount owing is within its jurisdictional limit; the order is taken to be an order of that court (s 121)`
#ASSERT `Where can I enforce my VCAT order` TRUE 100001 100000 EQUALS `in the County Court or the Supreme Court; the order is taken to be an order of the court I choose (s 121)`
#ASSERT `Where can I enforce my VCAT order` FALSE 0 100000 EQUALS `in the Supreme Court; the order is taken to be an order of the Supreme Court (s 122)`

§§ `s 148 -- appeals`

#ASSERT `Where does my appeal go` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `to the Trial Division of the Supreme Court, with the leave of the Trial Division, on a question of law (s 148(1)(b))`
#ASSERT `Where does my appeal go` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `to the Court of Appeal, with the leave of the Court of Appeal, on a question of law (s 148(1)(a))`
#ASSERT `Where does my appeal go` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered: section 148 gives an appeal on a question of law`

